From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: rk3528: Offer 12 and 24 kHz

The RK3528 datasheet lists 12 and 24 kHz among the codec's rates, which
SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000_192000 leaves out. Offer them.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/rk3528_codec.c b/sound/soc/codecs/rk3528_codec.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/rk3528_codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/rk3528_codec.c
@@ -502,7 +502,8 @@
 			.stream_name = "HiFi Playback",
 			.channels_min = 1,
 			.channels_max = 2,
-			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000_192000,
+			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000_192000 |
+				 SNDRV_PCM_RATE_12000 | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_24000,
 			.formats = (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE |
 				    SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |
 				    SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE),
